# JF Self Defense — one canonical host.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# -------------------
# Hostinger serves this docroot for BOTH www.jfselfdefense.com and
# jfselfdefense.com. Until this file, both returned 200, so every page on the
# site existed at two addresses and Google had two of everything to reconcile.
#
# The <link rel="canonical"> in BaseLayout already points at the non-www host,
# which is why this was a warning rather than an emergency — Google would very
# probably have consolidated on its own. Two things made it worth fixing anyway:
#
#   1. The only two external links pointing at this site, from AvenueOne's
#      write-up, use http://www.jfselfdefense.com/ — so whatever authority they
#      pass has been landing on the duplicate.
#   2. The Search Console property is the URL-prefix https://jfselfdefense.com/,
#      which does not cover www AT ALL. Anything arriving on the www host has
#      been invisible in the only place we measure.
#
# Non-www is canonical because that is what the canonical tags, the sitemap, the
# GSC property and the schema all already say. This file makes the server agree
# with them rather than the other way round.
#
# NO LOOP: the condition matches only the www host, and the target is the
# non-www host, which cannot match it again.
#
# Everything else about how this site is served is left alone on purpose —
# LiteSpeed's defaults for compression, caching and TLS are fine, and a
# speculative pile of headers here would be untested config on a live site.
# /admin/ keeps its own .htaccess; this rule runs before it and is what makes
# the admin reachable on one host too.

<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On

  # www -> bare domain, preserving path and query string, permanently.
  RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^www\.jfselfdefense\.com$ [NC]
  RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://jfselfdefense.com/$1 [R=301,L]

  # US spelling of the legal hub. It 404'd while still taking impressions at
  # position 1 in Search Console (2026-09-04, 09-16). Added 2026-09-22.
  RewriteRule ^articles/self-defense-law-singapore/?$ https://jfselfdefense.com/articles/self-defence-law-singapore/ [R=301,L]
</IfModule>

# Branded 404 (src/pages/404.astro) instead of Hostinger's generic page. Added 2026-09-22.
# NOTE: CI deploys with `scp -r dist/*`, which skips root dotfiles, so this file
# must be uploaded to the server by hand whenever it changes.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
